<Post title="Guaranteed delivery: paper and sources" description="Exact maxima and explicit attaining constructions, with the research manuscript, reproducible certificates, sources and Lean development." updated={release.publication_date}>
  <p><a href="/cop-prisoner/">Exact-count overview</a> · <a href="/cop-prisoner/proofs/">Classification proofs</a> · <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/">Lean coverage</a> · <a href="/cop-prisoner/delivery-time/">Delivery-time companion</a></p>
  <p><strong>Guaranteed indirect delivery in directed networks</strong><br/>Exact maxima and explicit attaining constructions.</p>
  <p>This is a {release.pages}-page research checkpoint with {release.figures} figures. Its central problem is the exact maximum <i>M(n,m)</i> for every <i>n ≥ 1</i> and <i>0 ≤ m ≤ n(n − 1)</i>, together with concrete adjacency rules or a specified attaining composition whose parameters are determined from <i>(n,m)</i>. Certified listed finite graphs qualify. The full joint table is complete through order seven; every final dense-band cell is exact; and every budget from 22 onward has its exact value and an explicit attaining graph at every order from eleven. At order eleven, the boundary values for budgets 22, 23 and 24 are 79, 78 and 79. Vertex-only and arc-only maxima follow as consequences. <strong>The complete classification remains open.</strong> The manuscript has not been submitted to arXiv.</p>
  <p>The uniform formula <i>M(n,m) = n(n − 1) − m</i> holds for every <i>n ≥ 12</i> and <i>2n ≤ m ≤ n(n − 3)</i>, with a sharp order threshold. Fixed staged certificates, six-offset circles and a reduced hub interface connect smaller orders to the retained infinite constructions. Smaller missing-pair intervals include budgets 24–26 at order eight, 24–54 at order nine, 28–70 at order ten and 25–88 at order eleven. The remaining {release.classification_coverage.representatives.toLocaleString('en-US')} representative pairs comprise {release.classification_coverage.small_budget.toLocaleString('en-US')} sparse, {release.classification_coverage.main.toLocaleString('en-US')} main-interval and {release.classification_coverage.dense.toLocaleString('en-US')} dense cases. All main gaps have orders eight through ten, and every remaining numerical question has a representative on at most eighteen stations.</p>
  <p>The <a href="/cop-prisoner/#explicit-constructions">explicit-construction inventory</a> is separate from the numerical coverage. Its family-by-family audit identifies a direct recipe or certified listed graph for every currently incorporated exact value; no known-value construction-only gap was found. This is a separate audit conclusion, not an inference from the eventual threshold or the finite reduction. An existence theorem alone does not complete the construction requirement.</p>
  <p>The final dense staircase has sharp threshold eleven and explicit attaining graphs within four moves throughout that range. The earlier two-move guarantee still covers the complete band from order sixteen. Smaller finite exceptions retain their own bounds, including five moves at nine stations and 55 arrows. Delivery-time optimization is retained in a separate <a href="/cop-prisoner/delivery-time/">parked companion</a>, with proved and partial results distinguished.</p>
